- How would you measure fairness and starvation in a multi-tenant system?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests dynamic plugin architecture, streaming parsing, and runtime extensibility without recompiling the core pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Plugin registry pattern using Factory/Strategy design
- Streaming I/O with backpressure-aware adapters
- Runtime extensibility and loose coupling for testability

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Parser {
  parse(input: AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>): AsyncIterable<Record<string, unknown>>;
}

type ParserFactory = () => Parser;

class Registry {
  private factories = new Map<string, ParserFactory>();

  register(extension: string, factory: ParserFactory): void {
    this.factories.set(extension.toLowerCase(), factory);
  }

  getParser(extension: string): Parser | undefined {
    return this.factories.get(extension.toLowerCase())?.();
  }
}

// Usage example
const registry = new Registry();
registry.register('xml', () => new XmlParser());
registry.register('yaml', () => new YamlParser());
registry.register('avro', () => new AvroParser());

async function processFile(path: string, data: AsyncIterable<Uint8Array>) {
  const ext = path.split('.').pop();
  const parser = registry.getParser(ext);
  if (!parser) throw new Error(`Unsupported format: ${ext}`);

  for await (const record of parser.parse(data)) {
    // Process record with backpressure handling
    await processRecord(record);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates ability to design runtime-extensible components and understand trade-offs when swapping strategies without downtime.

## Key Concepts

- Registry pattern
- Strategy/Policy pattern
- Concurrency control
- Observability

## Code Example

```typescript
interface EvictionPolicy<K> {
  onGet(key: K): void;
  onPut(key: K, value: unknown): void;
  evictIfNeeded(): K | null;
}

type EvictionPolicyFactory<K> = () => EvictionPolicy<K>;

class Registry<K> {
  private store = new Map<string, EvictionPolicyFactory<K>>();
  register(name: string, factory: EvictionPolicyFactory<K>) { this.store.set(name, factory); }
  create(name: string): EvictionPolicy<K> | null { const f = this.store.get(name); return f ? f() : null; }
}

class Cache<K, V> {
  private data = new Map<K, V>();
  private policy: EvictionPolicy<K> | null = null;
  constructor(private registry: Registry<K>, initialPolicy?: string) {
    if (initialPolicy) this.policy = registry.create(initialPolicy);
  }
  put(k: K, v: V) { this.data.set(k, v); this.policy?.onPut(k, v); if (this.policy) this.policy.evictIfNeeded(); }
  get(k: K): V | undefined { this.policy?.onGet(k); return this.data.get(k); }
  setPolicy(name: string) { const p = this.registry.create(name); if (p) this.policy = p; }
}
```

